r and writer, he was deeply involved in monastic methods and in integrating Zen realization into daily life. At times The Shobogenzo was profoundly difficult, and he worked on it over his entire life, revising and expanding, producing a book that is today thought to be one of the highest manifestations of Buddhist thought ever produced. Dogen's Genjo Koan is the first chapter in that book, and for many followers it might be thought to contain the gist of Dogen's work-it is one of the groundwork texts of Zen Buddhism, standing easily alongside The Diamond Sutra, The Heart Sutra, and a small handful of others.  Our unique edition of Dogen's Genjo Koan (Actualization of Reality) contains three separate translations and several commentaries by a wide variety of Zen masters. Nishiari Bokusan, Shohaku Okamura, Shunryu Suzuki, Kosho Uchiyama. Sojun Mel Weitsman, Kazuaki Tanahashi, and Dairyu Michael Wenger all have contributed to our presentation of this remarkable work. There can be no doubt that understanding and integrating this text will have a profound effect on anyone's life and practice\"--"},"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223101809482"],"lc_classifications":["BQ9449.D654 S53213 2011","BQ9449.D654S53213"],"key":"/books/OL25149194M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2782083A","name":"Dōgen Zenji"}],"publish_places":["Berkeley"],"contributions":["Uchiyama, Kōshō, 1912-","Okumura, Shohaku, 1948-"],"lccn":["2011011248"],"isbn_13":["9781582437439"],"pagination":"p. cm.","source_records":["marc:marc_loc_updates/v39.i52.records.utf8:53058837:2328","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run04.mrc:300866631:3551","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part38.utf8:172989285:2259","bwb:9781582437439","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.13.20150123.full.mrc:102373191:2478","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-019.mrc:81644505:2522","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_003.bib.mrc:175433160:3466"],"title":"Dogen Zenji's Shobogenzo Genjo-